            "answer": "32",
            "solution": "<div class=\"solution-content\"><a name=\"524824\"></a><div itemprop=\"text\"><p data-end=\"175\" data-start=\"121\">If a formula has <strong data-end=\"153\" data-start=\"138\">n variables</strong>, the truth table has:</p><p>2 ^n = no. of row </p><p data-end=\"239\" data-start=\"188\">rows because each variable can take <strong data-end=\"238\" data-start=\"224\">two values</strong>:</p><ul data-end=\"262\" data-start=\"240\"><li data-end=\"250\" data-section-id=\"17hheyz\" data-start=\"240\"><p data-end=\"250\" data-start=\"242\">True (T)</p></li><li data-end=\"262\" data-section-id=\"2w5cgi\" data-start=\"251\"><p data-end=\"262\" data-start=\"253\">False (F)</p></li><li data-end=\"262\" data-section-id=\"2w5cgi\" data-start=\"251\"><p data-end=\"262\" data-start=\"253\">For n = 5 </p></li><li data-end=\"262\" data-section-id=\"2w5cgi\" data-start=\"251\"><p data-end=\"262\" data-start=\"253\">no . of rows = 2^5 = 32 ans </p></li></ul></div><br><br><small>Source: <a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/524816/go-classes-dpp-gate-cs-discrete-mathematics-propositional-logic\" target=\"_blank\">GATE Overflow #524816</a></small></div>"
