            "solution": "<div class=\"solution-content\"><a name=\"524469\"></a><div itemprop=\"text\"><p>Note: a → b</p><p>we can say a is sufficient for b</p><p>or we can say b is necessary for a</p><hr/><p>given, \"To get an A in the class, it is necessary for you to get an A on the final\"</p><p>= P is necessary for R</p><p>= R → P</p><p>= ¬P → ¬R (contrapositive)</p><p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p></div><br><br><small>Source: <a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/524454/go-classes-dpp-gate-cs-discrete-mathematics-propositional-logic\" target=\"_blank\">GATE Overflow #524454</a></small></div>"
