            "marks": 1,
            "neg": 0,
            "type": "NAT",
            "text": "<span style=\"display: inline;\"><div itemprop=\"text\">Let:<br/> - $P$ : The server is running<br/> - $Q$ : The database is connected<br/> <br/> Interpret the following English statements carefully.<br/> <br/> Statement 1: \"The server or the database is active.\"<br/> <br/> Statement 2: \"Either the server or the database is active.\"<br/> <br/> Statement 3: \"The server or the database is active, but not both.\"<br/> <br/> Statement 4: \"At least one of the server and the database is active\"<br/> <br/> Select all correct options.<br/> <br/> A. Statement 1 is best translated as $P \\vee Q$<br/> B. Statement 2 is best translated as $P \\oplus Q$<br/> C. Statement 3 is best translated as $(P \\vee Q) \\wedge \\neg(P \\wedge Q)$<br/> D. Statement 4 is best translated as $P \\oplus Q$</div></span>",
            "image": "",
            "options": [],
            "answer": "524219",
            "solution": "<div class=\"solution-content\"><a name=\"524241\"></a><div itemprop=\"text\"><p data-path-to-node=\"0\"> </p><h2 data-path-to-node=\"1\"> </h2><p data-path-to-node=\"2\">Let:</p><ul data-path-to-node=\"3\"><li><p data-path-to-node=\"3,0,0\">$P$: The server is running</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"3,1,0\">$Q$: The database is connected</p></li></ul><hr data-path-to-node=\"4\"/><ul data-path-to-node=\"5\"><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,0,0\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"5,0,0\">Statement 1: \"The server or the database is active.\"</b></p><ul data-path-to-node=\"5,0,1\"><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,0,1,0,0\">In standard logic, \"or\" is <b data-index-in-node=\"27\" data-path-to-node=\"5,0,1,0,0\">Inclusive OR</b> ($\\lor$).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,0,1,1,0\">This includes the case where both are true.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,0,1,2,0\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"5,0,1,2,0\">Result: Option A is Correct ($P \\lor Q$)</b>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,1,0\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"5,1,0\">Statement 2: \"Either the server or the database is active.\"</b></p><ul data-path-to-node=\"5,1,1\"><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,1,1,0,0\">In formal logic, \"Either...or\" typically defaults to <b data-index-in-node=\"53\" data-path-to-node=\"5,1,1,0,0\">Inclusive OR</b> ($\\lor$) unless \"but not both\" is explicitly stated.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,1,1,1,0\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"5,1,1,1,0\">Result: Option B is Incorrect</b>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,2,0\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"5,2,0\">Statement 3: \"The server or the database is active, but not both.\"</b></p><ul data-path-to-node=\"5,2,1\"><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,2,1,0,0\">The phrase \"but not both\" forces the <b data-index-in-node=\"37\" data-path-to-node=\"5,2,1,0,0\">Exclusive OR (XOR)</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,2,1,1,0\">Logical form: $(P \\lor Q) \\land \\neg(P \\land Q)$.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,2,1,2,0\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"5,2,1,2,0\">Result: Option C is Correct</b>.</p></li></ul></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,3,0\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"5,3,0\">Statement 4: \"At least one of the server and the database is active\"</b></p><ul data-path-to-node=\"5,3,1\"><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,3,1,0,0\">\"At least one\" is the definition of <b data-index-in-node=\"36\" data-path-to-node=\"5,3,1,0,0\">Inclusive OR</b> ($\\lor$).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,3,1,1,0\">Option D incorrectly uses $P \\oplus Q$ (which means <i data-index-in-node=\"50\" data-path-to-node=\"5,3,1,1,0\">exactly</i> one).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=\"5,3,1,2,0\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"5,3,1,2,0\">Result: Option D is Incorrect</b>.</p></li></ul></li></ul><hr data-path-to-node=\"6\"/><h2 data-path-to-node=\"7\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"7\">Final Correct Options</b></h2><p data-path-to-node=\"8\"><b data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"8\">A and C</b></p></div><br><br><small>Source: <a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/524219/go-classes-dpp-gate-cs-discrete-mathematics-propositional-logic\" target=\"_blank\">GATE Overflow #524219</a></small></div>"
