            "solution": "<div class=\"solution-content\"><a name=\"523849\"></a><div itemprop=\"text\">Answer is option $D.\\frac{5}{2}$<br/> <br/> Let the G.P be $x=a,y=ar,z=ar^2$ <br/> <br/> A.P be $5a, 16ar,12ar^2$ <br/> <br/> $16ar-5a=12ar^2-16ar$ this will give us $12r^2-32r+5=0$<br/> <br/> this will give us $r=\\frac{1}{6},\\frac{5}{2}$ but since we are given that the GP is increasing order therefore $r&gt;1$<br/> <br/> Hence answer is option D.</div><br><br><small>Source: <a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/523824/go-classes-dpp-fundamental-of-computer-science-question-4\" target=\"_blank\">GATE Overflow #523824</a></small></div>"
